# Nothing here is built to be committed; the artifacts that have been signed are not source.
signed/
build/
dist/
*.spec

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Key material, in whatever form it appears. The engine hands out a public half (a .cer) on
# purpose, so that one is a decision to make rather than a default to inherit.
*.pfx
*.p12

# Scratch from a self-test run that was kept.
onlysign-selftest-*/

# The window's own settings: about one machine, not about the tool, and they name paths.
.onlysign/

# A notice of one's own. The repository ships a notice that belongs to nobody, and anyone may keep
# their real one here instead: it is read first, and it stays out of what gets published.
NOTICE.local*.txt


# The names a build belongs to: theirs, never the published tool.
IDENTITY.local.json

# WiX's UI extension, which the installer needs and which nobody should commit: it is a third-party
# binary from nuget.org. `tools/build-msi.py` names the path it expects and how to get it.
installer/extensions/

# The prepared art: the character sheet cut into poses, the standing figure, and the icon files it
# generates. Local, for the same reason the notices and the identity are -- the published tool is
# neutral, and the art belongs to its publisher. What is committed is the four files in mark/ that a
# build actually needs, not the working material behind them.
.onlysign-art/

# The toolchain under smyt/ is code. What makes it run -- the certificate, the password sealed in a
# container, the key that opens it, and the ledger of what has been signed -- is not code and does not
# belong in a repository, public or otherwise. The ledger most of all: it is a complete inventory of
# what has been signed and where each build sat on disk, which is a different kind of thing from a key.
#
# The pattern `*.pfx` above already covers one of these. This names the rest, so that "which files are
# the material" is answered here rather than by whoever last copied the directory in.
smyt/*.cer
smyt/*.sealed
smyt/*.key
smyt/*.ndjson
smyt/*.bak-*
smyt/.git/

# Where this machine keeps that material. Written down for the next session, not published: it names a
# path, and a path is about one machine rather than about the tool.
smyt/README.local.md
smyt/SIGNING-DIR.local.txt
